{
  "id": "30f7eb56-203b-4694-8a0e-20baa8186453",
  "page_title": "'Using your data with Azure OpenAI securely'",
  "page_description": "Use this article to learn about securely using your data for text generation in Azure OpenAI.",
  "page_date": "07/15/2024",
  "chunk_title": "Create resource group",
  "chunk_content": "Create resource group  Create a resource group, so you can organize all the relevant resources. The resources in the resource group include but are not limited to: * One Virtual network * Three key services: one Azure OpenAI, one Azure AI Search, one Storage Account * Three Private endpoints, each is linked to one key service * Three Network interfaces, each is associated with one private endpoint * One Virtual network gateway, for the access from on-premises client machines * One Web App with virtual network integrated * One Private DNS zone, so the Web App finds the IP of your Azure OpenAI",
